		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Incorrect DCS detected during scan]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4308&amp;p=32512#p32512"><![CDATA[
The hardware in these radios is not very good at detecting individual codes. The hardware generally works OK, if you select the code you are expecting to receive, and the squelch normally opens - unless perhaps the deviation of the signal is too high.<br><br>However when scanning for CTCSS/DCS codes, the hardware often gives false positives when receiving adjacent tones.<br><br>I don't know how DCS encoding works, or how the I and N codes work, but I suspect what you are experiencing are hardware limitations.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Thu Aug 15, 2024 3:00 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
